{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "description": "Mutations for the stored visual plan (slide.visual) and the gates that read the art capabilities, the icon data or the brand constraints: VA3 (kind, recipe, variant, icon, object, item counts), VA4, VA7, VA8, D10.glyph-icon and the C2 additions. Each patch plants a defect or a clean control on a fixture deck; `expect` lists the findings that must appear ({gate, rule, el or slide, sev?}) and the controls that must not ({absent: true}). The gates are implemented in JavaScript only until Q6 lands their Python twins, so run_js.mjs checks these entries against its own unfiltered findings and run_py.py skips them (qa-rules.json says who owns each check). The point is that the run cannot count a gate as executed while the capability data it needs is missing: with CS.visual.caps() empty, VA3 finds nothing for the impossible kind and recipe and these entries fail.",
 "mutations": [
  {
   "id": "vp-impossible-kind",
   "base": "spec.eg.8slides.json",
   "patch": [
    {"op": "add", "path": "/slides/2/visual", "value": {"anchor": {"kind": "scene", "template": "solo", "icons": ["camera"]}, "recipe": "under", "why": "مشهد"}},
    {"op": "add", "path": "/slides/4/visual", "value": {"anchor": {"kind": "icon", "icon": "camera"}, "recipe": "under", "why": "الكاميرا"}}
   ],
   "expect": [
    {"gate": "VA3", "rule": "VA3.valid", "el": "s03.anchor", "sev": "FIX"},
    {"gate": "VA3", "rule": "VA3.valid", "el": "s03.recipe", "absent": true},
    {"gate": "VA3", "rule": "VA3.valid", "el": "s05.anchor", "absent": true},
    {"gate": "VA3", "rule": "VA3.valid", "el": "s05.recipe", "absent": true}
   ]
  },
  {
